--  Caps.Delete_Cap is retired (#1023): petal deletes its own caps with
--  the Delete flag (#1022), and is given a null cap for the role. The
--  role stays because the supervisor sends petal its caps by position
--  (supervisor_loop.adb), and a supervisor is persistent: one installed
--  by an earlier release keeps sending this layout after an update.
command Rose.Core.Petal
  : Streams.Standard_IO, Caps.Create_Endpoint, Caps.Delete_Cap, Caps.Rescind_Cap, Commands.Find_Command,
    Screens.Console, Time.Clock_Service, Users.Rights_Service,
    Files.System_Directory
  with Summary     => "Run the shell for a user.",
       Description => """
          Petal is the shell. It runs the user's .petalrc, then reads
          commands from standard input and runs them, until the input
          ends, when it logs out and the command completes (#458).
          login runs it for each user who logs in (#457).
          """
is
   User : in Users.User
     with Help => "the user whose session this is";
end Rose.Core.Petal;
